{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospital doctors. You’ve just come up from the procedure area after your bronchoscopy. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hey, doc. I’m okay, still a bit groggy. My throat and trach site are sore, but nothing too bad yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. You had a routine bronchoscopy with balloon dilation to open up your trachea and bronchi. They also removed some granulation tissue that can cause narrowing. The procedure went smoothly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good, good. Was the dilation to the usual size?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they dilated the trachea and both main bronchi to your standard sizes—12 mm in the trachea, 10 mm on the left, 8 mm on the right. All stable compared to your last procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ve been having more wheezing lately, though. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chronic wheezing is expected due to your airway condition. We’ll monitor it. Right now, your lungs sound clear except for some baseline wheezing. No signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My pain’s starting to build. The 5 mg oxycodone doesn’t help much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll adjust that. We’re starting you on acetaminophen every 8 hours and ibuprofen every 6 hours as needed. For breakthrough pain, we’ll use 10 mg oxycodone every 4 hours as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds better. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We also checked your labs. Your white blood cell count is a bit high at 15.6, but that’s likely from the procedure or mild inflammation, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this time. It’s common after procedures. We’ll watch it and repeat the labs tomorrow. Your chest X-ray after the procedure showed no pneumothorax, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I heard something about a shadow on the X-ray?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, there was a new opacity at the right lung base. But you don’t have fever or increased sputum, so we don’t think it’s pneumonia. More likely a bit of atelectasis or minor aspiration. We’ll repeat the X-ray tomorrow to check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I’ve been on oxygen at home—should I keep that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re keeping your home oxygen going. Your saturation was 90% on room air earlier, so we’ll support you until we’re sure you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. What about my other meds? I didn’t bring my pirfenidone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. The hospital doesn’t have it in formulary, so we’re holding it for now. We’ll restart it when you get home. All your other meds—prednisone, losartan, pantoprazole—are continuing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. And the tobramycin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2139-01-09 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re continuing your inhaled tobramycin. It’s important for your lung health given your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I reviewed your repeat chest X-ray from this morning. The opacity in your right lung has cleared. No pneumonia or collapse. Great news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. How’s my pain looking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You rated it 4 out of 10 last night with the 10 mg oxycodone. We’ll keep the current plan for now and see if we can taper down by tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like to get off the opioids sooner if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re aiming for that. We’ll try reducing the oxycodone tomorrow if your pain stays under control with the other meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Sounds good. Any update on the biopsy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the tissue from your left main bronchus showed granulation tissue with organizing fibrin. No infection or cancer. That’s expected with your condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s just scar tissue building up again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s why you need regular dilations. It’s part of managing your syndrome and polychondritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2139-01-10 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2139-01-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs this morning look much better. White count is down to 8.0, hemoglobin is stable, and your electrolytes are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2139-01-11 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. How’s my pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2139-01-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You said it was 3 out of 10 last night and didn’t need any oxycodone after midnight. We’re going to stop the opioid now and just keep acetaminophen and ibuprofen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2139-01-11 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I feel ready for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2139-01-11 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, pharmacy noted your famotidine. We’ve been giving it at night instead of twice daily to avoid interaction with pantoprazole. You can go back to your regular dose at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2139-01-11 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll check with my PCP about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2139-01-11 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good idea. Otherwise, you’re doing really well. Lungs still wheezy but clear, walking independently, eating fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2139-01-12 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if all goes well. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2139-01-12 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Feeling great. No pain, breathing okay, and I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2139-01-12 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we like to hear. Your oxygen saturation is 100% on room air now, so you can stop supplemental oxygen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2139-01-12 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Excellent. Any restrictions when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2139-01-12 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just continue your normal activity. Avoid heavy lifting for a few days. Keep all your medications the same, including restarting pirfenidone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2139-01-12 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2139-01-12 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You already have an appointment scheduled with interventional pulmonary. They’ll coordinate your next dilation in about a month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2139-01-12 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2139-01-13 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your discharge orders are in. We’ll get you out within the next few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2139-01-13 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Just to confirm—same meds, same doses?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2139-01-13 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your home medications are continued: prednisone, losartan, pantoprazole, famotidine, pirfenidone, tobramycin, and supplements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2139-01-13 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll follow up with my doctors?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2139-01-13 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially with pulmonary and rheumatology. Call us if you develop fever, increased pain, breathing trouble, or redness at the trach site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2139-01-13 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again, doc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2139-01-13 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2139-01-13 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. Your vitals are stable: BP 129/80, heart rate 79, oxygen 100% on room air. You’re cleared to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2139-01-13 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Awesome. I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2139-01-13 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications one more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2139-01-13 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Appreciate the thoroughness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2139-01-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your biopsy confirmed granulation tissue, which explains the narrowing. No malignancy, so that’s very good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2139-01-13 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Relieved to hear that. Thanks for checking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2139-01-13 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Stay well, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2139-01-13 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Have a good one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2139-01-13 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you’ve received all your discharge paperwork and prescriptions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2139-01-13 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, everything’s in order. All set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2139-01-13 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Don’t hesitate to call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2139-01-13 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. Thanks again for the great care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2139-01-13 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Our pleasure. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2139-01-13 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, doc."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2139-01-09 21:12:00",
    "admission_end": "2139-01-13 13:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for post-procedural monitoring and pain control following an elective bronchoscopy with balloon dilation of the trachea and mainstem bronchi, along with debridement of granulation tissue, due to recurrent tracheobronchial stenosis from Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome and relapsing polychondritis. The procedure was uncomplicated, and he was managed with acetaminophen, ibuprofen, and oxycodone for pain, with successful weaning off opioids 24 hours before discharge. A transient right lung opacity noted on post-procedure imaging resolved without intervention and was not consistent with infection. Biopsy of the left mainstem lesion revealed benign granulation tissue without malignancy. His home medications were continued, except pirfenidone, which was held due to formulary restrictions. He remained stable, with improving lab values and no complications, and was discharged home in good condition with follow-up planned.",
    "problems": [
      "Other acute postprocedural pain",
      "Other specified congenital malformation syndromes, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other specified diseases of upper respiratory tract",
      "Other diseases of bronchus, not elsewhere classified",
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Elevated white blood cell count, unspecified",
      "Abnormal electrocardiogram [ECG] [EKG]",
      "Tracheostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
